Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:26:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep exact terminal releases across transport
 freshness gaps

Problem: an acked worker review stayed in a chat's Waiting list. The link
producer was not skipped: hub logs show default reconciliation every minute.
Live replay at epoch 1795241817 (last_ok age 160s) released the exact link;
at 1795241857 (same last_ok, age 200s) it demanded released=0 again.

Why 1: Waiting returned because reconciliation re-armed terminal chat links.
Why 2: the legacy projection turned done into unknown at transport age 180s.
Why 3: replacement discarded its previous release of the identical owner record.
Root (happened): transport freshness was incorrectly negative completion evidence.
Root (not caught): terminal tests covered fresh/stale reads independently, not
fresh -> stale through the actual links-pass producer and durable snapshot.
Recurrence: owner-silence release was fixed previously; global transport age
remained an independent re-arming path. The mail poller takes 3-5 minutes per
run plus a 60s cadence, exceeding the projection's 180s freshness window.
The ledger projection's created_at is projection time, not first-release time;
the original 47-minute one-way-lag inference is not established.

Preserve only a previously observed, verified terminal release with the same
validated raw owner-observation hash and full owner/chat identity. A changed,
reopened, tampered, unverified, cold stale or old tokenless record still waits.
The existing fresh-evidence gate for first release is unchanged. No ack policy,
SQLite schema, task lifecycle gate or replica freshness threshold is relaxed.

Proof: full reconcile_links regression is RED on parent (release 1 -> 0 at
+181s), GREEN with this patch. Regression includes real notice-ledger ack,
one-pass done release, restart persistence, identity and changed-proof controls.
Six focused consumer files passed 105 tests before the expanded identity matrix.

hotspot: hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py (two-line delegated call only).
